AB  - Dystonia is a syndrome of forceful, sustained muscle contractions, resulting in twisting and repetitive movements or abnormal postures. Dystonia is generally best understood as a clinical manifestation of disturbed basal ganglia physiology. Topics discussed include: prevalence of dystonia, clinical recognition and neurological presentation (forms and distribution of dystonia, initial signs and associated features, gender considerations and pregnancy, conversion disorder or dystonia?); pathological features; etiologies; neuroimaging; clinical and laboratory investigation; psychiatric manifestations (cognitive impairment, psychosis, mood disorders, anxiety disorders, eating disorders, somatoform disorders and psychogenic dystonia, substance abuse disorders, personality disorders, behavioral disorders, medication-induced psychiatric disorders); neurological management; and psychiatric management (general supportive treatment, pharmacological treatment, psychogenic dystonia). (PsycInfo Database Record (c) 2022 APA, all rights reserved)
