AB  - Presents a case study of a left-handed 18-year-old woman who developed a sudden total loss of normal speech production which was preceded by hoarseness. Here, we hypothesize that they have activated the depressed motor cortex with excitatory high-frequency repetitive transcranial magnetic stimulation (rTMS). On the contrary, in our aphonic patient, recovery was total with only one session of low-frequency rTMS. We have possibly blocked the active inhibition of the motor cortex with inhibitory low-frequency rTMS. This spectacular effect could also be explained by an important laryngeal muscular activation produced by the motor cortex stimulation and not by the prefrontal cortex stimulation. (PsycInfo Database Record (c) 2021 APA, all rights reserved)
