AB  - The etiology of medically unexplained symptoms such as medically unexplained paralysis (MUP) is poorly understood. This is partly because the interpretation of neuroimaging results in MUP has been complicated by the use of different control groups, tasks and statistical comparisons. The present study includes these different aspects in a single data set. The authors studied both movement execution and imagery, and we contrasted both within-group and between-group activation. Moreover, to increase clinical relevance by showing hemisphere-specific effects that have not been reported before the authors performed these analyses using both flipped and unflipped data. This approach revealed previously unidentified abnormal parietal underactivation which was specific for MUP. The patients showed reduced activity in the supramarginal gyrus (SG) and precuneus (SG), including hemisphere-specific activation that is lateralized in the same hemisphere, regardless of right or left sided paralysis. (PsycInfo Database Record (c) 2020 APA, all rights reserved)
