AB  - Comments on an article by Maryam Ejareh dar and Richard AA Kanaan (see record [rid]2016-02552-001[/rid]). Our paper on resting state brain metabolism measured by positron emission tomography (PET) was included and discussed. We were most surprised to see that the authors of the review seem to have misunderstood the findings of our study, which concerned patients with psychogenic non-epileptic seizures (PNES). The authors state that the 16 patients included in our study “were later found to have PNES with comorbid epilepsy”. This is incorrect, since our study included only patients with PNES in whom comorbid epilepsy was excluded. We certainly agree with the authors regarding the importance of reviewing the literature on this complex subject, and the need for further studies with more rigorous methodology. (PsycInfo Database Record (c) 2025 APA, all rights reserved)
