AB  - Reply by the current authors to the comments made by Francesco Brigo (see record [rid]2017-10087-025[/rid]) on the original article (see record [rid]2016-57261-002[/rid]). The authors thank Brigo for his interest in and feedback on their article. It is reasonable to speculate that some of the ambivalence in communicating the diagnosis of psychogenic non-epileptic seizures (PNES) by some providers may be due to a lack of understanding of the associated neurophysiologic mechanisms of PNES. The authors agree that despite there being a number of studies describing functional and structural neuroimaging, serologic, cardiac, and electrophysiologic markers in patients with functional neurologic disorders/conversion disorders, a unifying neurophysiologic explanation for conversion disorder does not exist. (PsycInfo Database Record (c) 2025 APA, all rights reserved)
