AB  - This pilot voxel-based morphometry (VBM) study used a within-group design to investigate the relationship between baseline volumetric profiles and prospectively collected 6-month outcome data in 22 patients with FND. Stratified comparative analyses with 27 controls were performed to contextualise statistically significant within-group findings. Based on the outcome literature and previously described corticolimbic associations with health status and adverse life events, we hypothesised that baseline amygdalar– hippocampal and cingulo-insular volumes would predict clinical outcomes in FND. Methods Methods were adapted from Perez et al. Participants Twenty-two subjects with FND (19 women, 3 men; age=41.7±11.0 years; illness duration=3.9±4.6 years) were recruited from the Massachusetts General Hospital (MGH) FND Clinic with baseline (MRI+psychometric data) and follow-up copyright. (PsycInfo Database Record (c) 2024 APA, all rights reserved)
