AB  - Comments on an article by A. A. Asadi-Pooya et al. (see record [rid]2020-18949-001[/rid]) on terminology for psychogenic nonepileptic seizures (PNES). Although we concur with Asadi-Pooya et al. sustaining that “<i>it is clearly not ideal to define a disorder by what it is not. Such negative terms provide no relevant positive information regarding the disorder in terms of what it is</i>”, we are not interested in proposing a new acronym for PNES, but we would like to point out the contribution of neuroimaging in featuring this condition. What we recommend is to put more effort in sustaining the neuroimaging community and its findings. In other words, we need to share data that can allow us to (really) understand what PNES or whatever the term means, by a biological point of view. (PsycInfo Database Record (c) 2025 APA, all rights reserved)
