AB  - The present study aimed to assess the amygdala through histogram analysis using T1-weighted magnetic resonance imaging (MRI) images of patients with Functional Neurological Disorder (FND) and to compare the findings with healthy controls. Twenty female patients, who applied to the psychiatry outpatient clinic consequently and diagnosed with FND based on Diagnostic and statistical Manual of Mental Disorders-5 criteria, were included in the study. Study criteria included 18-65 years of age, no other psychiatric diagnosis or mental retardation, no neurological or physiological disease, alcohol or substance abuse history during the last 6 months, and no MRI examination contraindications. Twenty healthy female individuals, who fulfilled the study criteria without a psychiatric, neurological or physiological disease, or a history of medical treatment and contraindications for MRI examination, were included in the control group. The Local Ethics Committee approval was obtained. All participants signed an informed consent form and MRI scan was conducted. The findings demonstrated that other functional anatomic structures should be investigated with a similar method. (PsycInfo Database Record (c) 2022 APA, all rights reserved)
