to diagnosis and care. Our discussion explores the limited but evolving literature on postpartum FND—potentially inclusive of sensory-motor mismatch, loss of agency, hormonal shifts, and psychosocial stressors—while also exploring strategies for culturally grounded psychoeducation. Clinicians must vigilantly watch for functional presentations postpartum to avoid unnecessary interventions and promote holistic recovery. Cross-disciplinary collaboration among psychiatry, neurology, and obstetrics is essential for optimal care. (PsycInfo Database Record (c) 2026 APA, all rights reserved)
