AB  - Dynamic Test Case Prioritization in Continuous Integration and Continuous Delivery (CI/CD) is difficult under scarce historical data and rapidly changing code. The DynaPrior framework addresses these conditions with a unified design that combines meta-learning for fast cross-project adaptation, contrastive embeddings for discriminative test representations, an ACER-based reinforcement-learning scheduler for online reordering, and neuro-symbolic overrides for auditable, risk-aware promotion of critical tests. Evaluation on Apache Commons, Mozilla Core, and an industrial mobile suite reports APFD = 94.2% (up to +6.7% over baselines), FDS = 35.4 s (≈27% faster than Learn-to-Rank), PET = 120.5 s (≈21% faster than Learn-to-Rank), PO = 1.8 s (>40% lower than Learn-to-Rank), and stability ρ = 0.94; all pairwise differences versus baselines are statistically significant under the Section 4 testing plan. The integration yields interpretable, low-overhead decisions suitable for deployment in practical CI/CD pipelines where rapid adaptation and transparent justification are required.
