AU  - Dhareshwar S.
AU  - Alwbaidy M.
AU  - Verma A.K.
AU  - Patel K.
AU  - Mahalakshmi G.
PY  - 2025
JO  - 2nd International Conference on Intelligent Algorithms for Computational Intelligence Systems Iacis 2025
SN  - [9798331536770]
AB  - The role of early diagnosis of any medical condition is crucial and with the advancement of medical science and technology, the need for a smart and effective diagnosis is significant. However, to train the model for better efficiency, the model requires a large amount of data, but legal, ethical, and patient privacy issues challenge the sharing of datasets between different centers. Therefore, to address these issues, this research proposes an architecture, namely FDS-RFP, which is a federated learning framework that integrates a Recursive Feature Pyramid (RFP) and Diagonal Shifted-Window Vision Transformer (DiagSWin) with a differential privacy mechanism. The objective is to enhance lesion localization across multiscale medical imagery, while ensuring data confidentiality in decentralized environments. The methodology involves dual-stream feature extraction from the original and preprocessed medical images, recursive extraction of multiscale embeddings through RFP, and contextual encoding through DiagSWin attention modules. An adaptive Customer Performance Value (CPV) mechanism selectively aggregates updates from high-performance clients, preserves privacy, and improves framework's convergence. Numerical validations were conducted on NIH ChestX-ray14, Shenzhen CXR, and BR35H MRI medical datasets, this framework achieved 99.8%, 99.3%, 99.6% for NIH ChestX-ray 14, Br35H brain MRI, and Shenzhen dataset respectively, outperforming existing baselines in both classification performance and privacy preservation.
DO  - 10.1109/iacis65746.2025.11210954
