AB  - Functional Neurological Disorder (FND) is a brain-based condition affecting cognition, emotion, and sensorimotor behaviors. FND is associated with biological, psychological, and sociodevelopmental risk factors. There are several clinical subtypes, including functional nonepileptic seizures, functional movement disorders, functional cognitive disorder, and persistent postural-perceptual dizziness, to name a few. Structural and functional connectivity differences on neuroimaging have been revealed in the brains of those living with FND compared to control groups. Evidence-based interventions include psychotherapy, rehabilitative therapies, and a multidisciplinary treatment approach. Neuromodulation is undergoing study and may play a future role in the treatment of FND.
